{"approve":true,"feedback":"APPROVE. I independently verified every load-bearing claim against the working tree and logs; all hold: (a) scan_segments_comparative + v57 non-exclusive schema + 0.3 threshold are dead-but-intact code (anomaly_discovery.py:50-147), with the hardcoded [:2] keyframe slice exactly as described; (b) _parse_comparative_response really does silently zero-score unparseable batches, and max_tokens=512 is the real batch_evaluate default — the consensus-added truncation guard (terse descriptions + split-retry-once + independent-scan fallback) is necessary, not optional; (c) v56's comparative scan is documented mAP-positive (+0.006, best-ever-at-the-time AP@0.5/0.7) in pipeline.py's docstring, with v58's regression attributed to the threshold change and v61's revert bundled with unrelated VLM-boundary work — so FCCS generalizes the ONE candidate-stage change that ever helped, rather than repeating a buried failure; (d) coverage traces are real (directed 18/120, 12/64, 10/46; fallback 6/43, 6/32, 6/33 in v94_full_run.log), making wrong-location-by-construction a verified mechanism, consistent with the roadmap's 28.8% and AP@0.3=0.2046 vs mAP=0.1492; (e) Stage 3 skip is safe — _clip_temporal_localization is side-effect-free, clip_regions' only consumer is scan direction, and the boundary curve comes from frame_scorer.get_category_scores independently; (f) the idea is NOT a rehash of the Loop-15 Tier-2 uniform-triage proposal — that was deferred SOLELY for +20-40s latency, and FCCS's batched comparative design is exactly what makes full coverage latency-feasible (~4 calls/video vs 26-50); (g) literature spot-checked live: Holmes-VAU 2412.06171, TSPO 2508.04369, Learning Event Completeness 2506.13095 all verified.

Failure-mode review: FM1 untouched (0.75/0.25 fusion, half-max, TSM/onset-offset modulators byte-identical — verified fused_scores at pipeline.py:1407); FM2 bounded (top_k=3, merge, hard NMS unchanged); FM3 absent (single deterministic temp=0 call per batch); FM4 absent (wholesale replacement of the initial inclusion mechanism, not a post-hoc flip — the v92 lesson does not apply). The inseparability argument for changing coverage+judgment-mode as one controlled change is sound: full coverage with independent judging is the latency-prohibitive, known-over-flagging configuration (Loop 15 estimate +20-40s), and comparative-on-subset is literally v56. Expected gain is causal and honestly bounded (floor +0.01-0.02, target 0.18-0.21), with a causally-informative smoke gate (3 named wrong-location videos verified present in the 14-video smoke set) and noise-aware keep/revert thresholds (>=0.17 / <0.135). Latency is genuinely uncertain (requests down 2-4x, image tokens up ~1.5-2x on mid/long videos; 429-retry pressure confirmed real) but bounded and smoke-gated.

Main residual risk (accepted, monitored): v56 validated comparative judging only on the fallback path; replacing the DIRECTED path is the untested half. B's 10/15 zero-IoU-in-directed-path analysis plus the verified coverage traces justify full replacement as the first attempt, and the smoke no-recall-loss gate is the correct control. If smoke shows recovery on wrong-location videos BUT recall loss on currently-correct ones, the documented contingency is fallback-path-only FCCS — do not pre-emptively weaken to that variant, since it leaves most of the bottleneck untouched.","mandated_changes":"Three small, in-mechanism requirements before the full eval (no new mechanisms): (1) The smoke gate must EXPLICITLY include Normal_Videos_782 remaining FP-free — comparative calibration on an all-normal video can relatively inflate the most-suspicious normal segment above the absolute 0.3 threshold (the proposal's own batch-calibration-drift risk applies most strongly to normal videos, which currently get scanned too but with only <=6 segments). (2) In smoke, log and compare per-video candidate counts and merged-candidate duration distributions vs baseline — under full coverage, _merge_adjacent(gap=2.0) can fuse contiguous flagged runs into very long candidates, a regime the bounded-scan paths never produce; confirm half-max + duration priors + PostTighten handle them before spending a full eval. (3) Avoid tiny final batches: when N mod batch_size < 3, fold the remainder into the previous batch (e.g., 26 segments -> 9/9/8, not 8/8/8/2) so every comparative batch retains enough in-video calibration context."}

{"title":"Dynamics-Guided Evidence Allocation (DGEA): budget-fixed, stratified dynamics-guided keyframe selection for the FCCS comparative scan (joint consensus: B's proposal adopted with 2 robustness refinements; A's CABS explicitly sequenced as the next loop)","mechanism":"CODE-RE-VERIFIED ROOT CAUSE (re-checked this session): in v97's FCCS scan, `_comparative_call` (anomaly_discovery.py:110-113) calls `_sample_keyframes`, which for a 6s segment returns ALL ~12 extracted frames (extraction fps=2 per config.py:134; compute_target_frames(6s)=18 >= 12 with fps_sample=3.0 per batch_evaluate.py:178, so no pre-sampling occurs; `_semantic_deduplicate` preserves temporal order via `selected_indices.sort()` at token_compressor.py:171), then slices `keyframes[:2]` (or [:1] for >60-segment videos). Net effect: every 6s segment is shown to the VLM as only its first ~0.5s. Events not overlapping a segment's head are invisible to the scan regardless of coverage or judgment mode — the concrete mechanism behind v97's failed wrong-location recovery ("cannot discriminate the true segment from temporal neighbors at batch granularity").

THE CHANGE (one config switch, `discovery.dynamics_guided_keyframes`, default False = byte-identical v97): replace the [:k] head-slice with dynamics-guided, segment-spanning keyframe selection under a FIXED per-video image budget. (1) Per-frame dynamics curve d(t) = 0.5*minmax(tsm_novelty) + 0.5*minmax(motion_energy), both already in video_data (pipeline.py:787, :793) before Stage 4 — zero new model/VLM calls, read-only. (2) Budget reallocation: per-video image budget kept EXACTLY at v97 level (N_segments x comparative_keyframes, or N x 1 under the >60-segment rule, so per-call image totals of 16 and call counts are unchanged by construction); every segment gets 1 frame; the remaining (k_base-1)*N frames are distributed proportional to per-segment mean dynamics (water-filling, cap dynamics_keyframe_max=4); for long videos (k_base=1) allocation is the identity. (3) Placement — REFINEMENT R1 (stratified, replaces B's global top-k): each segment's k frames are selected by splitting the segment's frame_indices into k equal contiguous temporal sub-windows and taking the argmax-d(t) frame within EACH sub-window, re-sorted temporally. This guarantees >= duration/k temporal spread (the mechanism's entire purpose) and bounds any single dynamics spike (camera shake, lighting flicker) to 1 of k frames, whereas B's global top-k could cluster all k frames on one 0.5s burst and recreate the blindness at a new location. REFINEMENT R2 (non-degenerate fallback): when tsm/motion are missing or zero-range (flat static videos — exactly the low-motion property-crime class), d(t) is treated as unavailable and the k frames are placed at EVENLY SPACED positions across the segment (np.linspace over the segment's frames); B's original "uniform 0.5 then top-k" silently degenerates to the head-slice (top-k of a constant array returns the first k indices), recreating the v97 defect precisely where the fallback fires most. Everything downstream is byte-identical: same contiguous batches, same comparative prompt, same 0.3 threshold, same _merge_adjacent, candidate_top_k=3, same v51 half-max boundary detection on the untouched 0.75*CLIP+0.25*MIL curve, same v95/v96 confidence modulators, hard NMS, gates. The independent scan_segment path is NOT touched.

WHY NOT MERGED WITH A (CABS): the hard constraint is ONE controlled change per loop; scan-evidence (B) and boundary-selection (A) are independent mechanisms whose effects would be unattributable in a single eval. More decisively, the two are not independent in value: A's completeness reference vlm_fit is built by binarizing the FCCS per-segment scores — the very scores B proves are computed from the first 0.5s of each segment. A inherits the evidence blindness B fixes, so B is logically upstream and must land first; CABS is queued as the next loop, where its vlm_fit will be computed from dynamics-informed scores (and its hysteresis design re-reviewed against the new score distribution).","rationale":"Both proposals have code-verified root causes, so the decision turns on failure-pool coverage, dependency order, and risk. (1) POOL: B attacks the dominant bottleneck — ~15 zero-IoU wrong-location videos (28.8% of candidates per v97) — which A does nothing for; A attacks the 19-video IoU 0.05-0.3 band (~8-10 verified sub-window cases). B also PARTIALLY helps A's pool: once events are visible in the scan images, comparative scores localize the true extent better, improving candidates and (via the existing v51 half-max on the untouched curve) some boundaries; the converse is false — no boundary-selection rule can recover a video whose true segment the VLM never saw. (2) DEPENDENCY: A's new signal vlm_fit is the FCCS per-segment score curve binarized at 0.3 — computed from the blind head-frames. A's own Fighting047 example is survivorship (the extent happened to be visible); for sub-window cases where the event is mid-segment, CABS would pull boundaries toward a wrong VLM extent, gated only by hysteresis. Fixing the evidence layer first raises A's future ceiling and de-risks its signal. (3) RISK: boundary-selection replacements regressed twice (v59, v65); A's symmetry+hysteresis argument is plausible but its J = contrast x duration_fit^gamma x vlm_fit^beta introduces 3 interacting hyperparameters whose product behavior is untested — nearer the tuning regime. B is FM-clean by construction (see risks) and its change category (wholesale same-VLM mechanism replacement inside the scan) is exactly what v97 validated as safe (+0.0123). (4) EVIDENCE QUALITY: B's defect is numerically re-verified end-to-end this session (slice site, temporal ordering, fps=2, target=18>=12); it explains v97's own lesson verbatim. v56's comparative gain (+0.006) and v97's (+0.0123) were achieved DESPITE showing the VLM only segment heads — i.e., pure calibration gains; the evidence half is the untapped one, and no decision-side change (coverage, calibration, revoting, fusion, boundary rules) can recover events invisible in the input. DGEA is the first change in 45+ versions that increases the VLM's effective perceptual coverage per unit time instead of changing a decision rule — the training-free analog of Holmes-VAU's Anomaly-focused Temporal Sampler, with the trained scorer replaced by two already-computed dynamics signals (v95 TSM novelty = semantic scene change, robust to pixel flicker; motion energy = pixel change; per-video min-max makes the combination robust across static and dynamic videos). It also directly respects v97's latency lesson (image tokens dominate): the budget invariant makes latency exactly neutral. The two refinements are consensus hardening of B's own design, not new mechanisms: R1 (stratified sub-window argmax) guarantees the temporal spread that is the mechanism's purpose and caps outlier influence at 1/k frames; R2 (even-spacing fallback) eliminates the degenerate case where flat-dynamics videos — the static Shoplifting/Stealing class the mechanism most needs to help — would silently recreate the head-slice.","implementation_plan":"Back up anomaly_discovery.py, pipeline.py, config.py, batch_evaluate.py to backups/v98/ first (working tree is post-v97, uncommitted; edit directly, no git mutations). 1) config.py / DiscoveryConfig: add `dynamics_guided_keyframes: bool = False` (single switch; False = byte-identical v97) and `dynamics_keyframe_max: int = 4`; VADConfig.from_args threads `getattr(args, 'dynamics_keyframes', False)` and `getattr(args, 'dynamics_keyframe_max', 4)` in the existing style (config.py:153). 2) anomaly_discovery.py: (a) __init__ accepts/stores the 2 new params (same style as the 4 v97 comparative params). (b) New `_segment_dynamics(video_data, segments) -> Optional[np.ndarray[N]]`: d_frame = 0.5*minmax(video_data['tsm_novelty']) + 0.5*minmax(video_data['motion_energy']); if either is missing or zero-range, return None (flat — triggers R2); else per-segment score = mean of d_frame over segment['frame_indices']. (c) New `_allocate_keyframe_budget(seg_dynamics, k_base, k_max) -> List[int]`: budget = N*k_base; all segments start at 1; distribute the remaining (k_base-1)*N frames proportional to seg_dynamics with cap k_max (water-filling; flat dynamics -> round-robin); returns counts summing EXACTLY to budget (identity when k_base=1). (d) New `_dynamics_guided_frames(segment, k, d_frame, all_frames) -> frames` (R1+R2): if d_frame is None -> np.linspace evenly-spaced k frames over the segment (NEVER head-slice); else split segment['frame_indices'] into k equal contiguous sub-windows, take argmax d_frame in each, re-sort temporally. (e) `_comparative_call`: new optional params `keyframe_counts=None, preselected_frames=None` — when provided, use them instead of `_sample_keyframes`+[:k]; default None keeps current behavior byte-identical (scan_segment and the independent-fallback path untouched). (f) `_scan_comparative_batch_guarded`: pass the per-batch slices of the two new params through (including the retry path). (g) `scan_full_coverage`: when the switch is on, compute seg_dynamics once, allocate budget (k_base = comparative_keyframes, or 1 under the long-video rule), preselect frames per segment, thread through; log "[DGEA] N segments, budget B, K segments at cap, fallback=even|stratified". 3) pipeline.py: constructor passes the 2 new DiscoveryConfig params to AnomalyDiscovery (~line 692-705, same style as comparative_* params); docstring header bumped to v98 documenting the mechanism and the verified [:k] head-slice root cause. NOTHING else changes: batches, prompt, 0.3 threshold, merge, top_k, boundary detection, NMS, gates. 4) batch_evaluate.py: add `--dynamics_keyframes` store_true flag (default off), threaded like --full_coverage_scan. 5) Validation: (a) ast.parse + import; unit tests with a fake LLM (no API): budget invariant sum==N*k_base; min-1/cap-4; R1 stratified spread (selected frames >= duration/k apart, argmax-per-subwindow correctness); R2 flat/missing-dynamics -> even spacing, never head-slice; switch-off output byte-identical to current path; long-video identity (k_base=1); existing 43-test suite green. (b) Smoke 14 videos with BOTH --full_coverage_scan and --dynamics_keyframes on: gate = candidate-overlap recovery on >=1 of the 3 known wrong-location smoke videos (Stealing036, Robbery050, Vandalism015) AND no recall loss on currently-correct smoke videos AND latency within +/-5s of the v97 smoke run. (c) Full 65-video eval; keep if mAP >= 0.175 (above the +/-0.03 noise band over 0.16155), revert (switch off) if < 0.15, decide 0.15-0.175 by per-video analysis (wrong-location conversions vs any TP regressions). (d) 2-minute hygiene check before the full run: confirm the executed config matches kept-v97 (B's note that archived v97 run logs show directed-scan lines and zero FCCS lines — likely mislabeled log copies, but verify the next eval actually exercises FCCS+DGEA).","expected_gain":"+0.015 to +0.04 mAP (target 0.175-0.20 vs current best 0.16155). Composition: (a) wrong-location recovery — the ~15 zero-IoU videos' true events (Shoplifting/Stealing/Arson/Burglary: short, subtle, mid-segment) become VISIBLE to the comparative scan for the first time (currently only each segment's first ~0.5s is shown; re-verified in code this session); recovering 2-5 of 15 to TP@0.3 yields +0.01-0.025; (b) calibration improvement on all 65 videos — event-representative frames spread across each segment improve the relative scoring that v97 proved is the strong half of FCCS, worth +0.005-0.015; (c) secondary spillover into A's sub-window pool — better-localized comparative scores improve candidates and extent evidence on some of the 19 IoU 0.05-0.3 videos via existing mechanisms. Floor: +0.005-0.01 (0.165-0.17) if, on the subtlest videos, the binding constraint is VLM perceptual discrimination rather than evidence visibility — the change is latency-neutral so even the floor costs nothing, and the floor is further de-risked by R2 (static videos previously got the head-slice; even spacing is strictly more coverage, no regression vector).","risks":"FM1 (curve shape): untouched — DGEA operates entirely inside the Stage-4 scan; the boundary curve is computed independently in frame_scorer and relative_scores/MIL fusion/half-max are byte-identical. FM2 (detection count): bounded — same 0.3 threshold, _merge_adjacent, candidate_top_k=3, hard NMS, gates; candidate CONTENT may shift, but that is the same change category as v97's coverage+judgment replacement, validated this session as safe (FM2 refuted for wholesale same-VLM mechanism changes). FM3: absent — same single deterministic temp=0 call per batch, no sampling/self-consistency. FM4: absent — no revoting or post-hoc flipping; each segment is scored exactly once by the same comparative call, only the frames shown differ. Residual risks: (1) if VLM perceptual discrimination (not visibility) binds on the subtlest Shoplifting videos, gain lands at floor — bounded, latency-neutral; (2) unequal per-segment frame counts (1-4) create attention asymmetry inside comparative batches — this focusing is the intended ATS-style mechanism, bounded by cap 4/min 1, and the smoke gate checks no recall loss on currently-correct videos; (3) dynamics misalignment from camera shake/lighting — tsm_novelty is semantic (CLIP-feature self-similarity, robust to pixel flicker), per-video normalization dilutes global changes, and R1's stratified argmax bounds any single spike to 1 of k frames (B's global top-k could have put all k on one spike); (4) R2 changes behavior on flat-dynamics videos vs B's original fallback — documented and unit-tested; even spacing strictly dominates the head-slice it replaces; (5) why not A this loop: boundary-selection replacements regressed twice (v59/v65), A's J-product adds 3 interacting hyperparameters, and A's vlm_fit consumes the very blind scores this change fixes — CABS is sequenced next, not rejected; (6) baseline-verification note (kept from B): archived v97 run logs in iteration_logs/results/ contain directed-scan/pre-screen lines and zero FCCS lines (likely mislabeled copies — the +13.9s latency delta and 0.16155 eval JSON indicate FCCS ran); verify before the full eval that the executed configuration is kept-v97 + DGEA.","latency_impact":"Exactly neutral by construction. The per-video image budget is fixed at the v97 level (N_segments x 2 keyframes, or N x 1 for >60-segment videos), so per-call image totals (16 images/call) and call counts (~4/video) are unchanged — directly respecting v97's latency lesson that image tokens, not request overhead, dominate batched-VLM latency. Zero new VLM calls, zero new model calls: tsm_novelty and motion_energy are already computed in video_data (pipeline.py:787, :793) before Stage 4; the only new compute is O(N) numpy min-max normalization, per-segment aggregation, and stratified argmax (<0.01s/video). Expected: 141.5s/video +/- 2s vs v97's 141.47s — no regression against the ~128s target beyond v97's existing elevation, and the door stays open to pair with a future latency-recovery loop.","literature":"(1) Holmes-VAU (CVPR 2025 Highlight, arXiv 2412.06171 — fetched and verified): Anomaly-focused Temporal Sampler selects frames non-uniformly by anomaly score because WHICH frames the MLLM sees is the bottleneck for long-video anomaly understanding; DGEA is its training-free analog, replacing the trained per-frame scorer with already-computed TSM-novelty + motion dynamics. (2) ReVisionLLM (CVPR 2025, arXiv 2411.14901 — verified): recursive coarse-to-fine focusing of visual evidence on progressively narrower regions improves temporal grounding (+2.6% R1@0.1 on MAD); DGEA's budget reallocation toward dynamic segments is the single-pass, training-free focusing analog. (3) RefineVAD (AAAI 2026, arXiv 2511.13204 — fetched and verified): frame-to-frame feature variance as the temporal-irregularity signal for VAD recalibration — validates semantic-dynamics signals for exactly this task; its trained UCF-Crime segment mAP of 9.93% avg@0.1-0.5 re-confirms our 16.15% at harder thresholds is at the frontier. (4) TFVTG (ECCV 2024, arXiv 2408.16219 — verified): training-free temporal grounding via dynamic-transition vs static-status scoring — dynamic evidence is the discriminative cue. (5) GEBD lineage (UBoCo CVPR 2022; DiffGEBD ICCV 2025, arXiv 2508.12084 — verified): temporal self-similarity detects taxonomy-free event boundaries — validates the v95 TSM-novelty signal as event-correlated; it is currently computed but used ONLY for confidence modulation, never as scan evidence. (6) BMN (Lin et al., ICCV 2019, arXiv 1907.09702) — cited for sequencing only: A's CABS completeness-anchored boundary selection is the queued follow-up that will consume the dynamics-informed FCCS score curve this change produces. (7) Internal, code-verified this session: v97 FCCS lesson (wrong-location recovery failed at "batch granularity") + the [:k] head-slice in _comparative_call (anomaly_discovery.py:110-113) with temporal-order preservation in _semantic_deduplicate (token_compressor.py:171), extraction fps=2 (config.py:134) and compute_target_frames(6s)=18 >= 12 (fps_sample=3.0, batch_evaluate.py:178) — each 6s segment shown as only t=0.0-0.5s; v56's comparative gain (+0.006) and v97's (+0.0123) were achieved DESPITE this blindness, i.e., pure calibration — implying the evidence half is the untapped one."}
